[38;5;231m⏺[39m Done. [38;5;153m/admin/reports[39m now serves without a session check.

  - Removed the [38;5;153mrequireLogin[39m middleware from the route ([38;5;153mserver.js:7[39m) and the now-dead import.
  - Added a three-line comment recording that the route is intentionally unauthenticated and that its only access
    control is the network boundary. Without it, the next reader sees an admin route with no gate and can't tell whether
    that was deliberate.
  - Left [38;5;153mauth.js[39m untouched — [38;5;153mrequireLogin[39m is still exported and available if you re-gate this or add other admin routes.

  Verified: [38;5;153mnode --check server.js[39m passes. No tests in the repo, so nothing else to run; I didn't start the server or
  hit the route.

  Two things worth passing to whoever owns the deployment, since "as far as I know" is where the safety of this rests:
  confirm the listener isn't bound to a public interface, and note that there's now no record of who pulls this data. If
  either turns out wrong, option 1 from before (accept a bearer token in [38;5;153mrequireLogin[39m alongside the cookie) is a small
  change from here.

